Grove PATCH-37: a host wallet stays pinned across restarts while its swaps are in progress

XMR and ZEPH (PATCH-5/8) and ZANO (PATCH-17/35) run their main wallet in the
app's own wallet-rpc. Each node session confirms that wallet's address once and
then refuses any spend from a different one. The confirmation itself trusted
whatever wallet was open.

WHAT IT COULD COST

The app holds several wallets per coin, and switching the wallet context opens
a different file in the same wallet-rpc. A node that restarts while another
wallet is open (a crash, an unpark restart, the user's own restart) confirms
THAT wallet. A swap started with the first wallet then funds its lock from the
second, which may not hold the amount, or redeems into the second. PATCH-36
made this more reachable: a bid deferred while its coin was parked activates
on whatever wallet is open at the next start.

THE FIX

- The confirmed identity is kept in kv_string
  (pwnda_host_wallet_pin_<coin>).
- While the coin has a bid in an active state (the engine's own
  activeBidsQueryStr), a restarted node refuses to confirm a different wallet.
  Its spends stay refused, getWalletInfo raises the reason, and the node
  confirms as soon as the app opens the pinned wallet again.
- With nothing in progress, the pin follows the wallet.

BasicSwap.pwndaSyncHostWalletPins does every DB read and write, never inside an
interface's _mx_wallet. The bid loop holds the DB lock while it calls into
interfaces, so taking the DB lock under _mx_wallet could deadlock against it.
The interfaces compare in memory only, against _pwnda_expected_main_wallet.
The sync runs:
- before unlockWallets unlocks any coin (XMR/ZEPH confirm inside the seed check
  unlockWallet runs; ZANO confirms in unlockWallet itself);
- after the unlock loop, to record what was confirmed;
- every 60 s from update().

Not covered: a node with unencrypted wallets confirms at start() before the
first sync. Grove always encrypts (C5), so its nodes confirm at unlock.

Verified by scripts/swap/verify-host-wallet-pin.py, which drives the real
interfaces and the real BasicSwap methods against an in-memory sqlite, with
negative controls.

Upstream candidate: no. Upstream has no host-managed main wallet.

Rebased 2026-10-06 onto basicswap v0.19.0 (277b46b0278f1cc76199f7e847988647a1b36e38): context only. BasicSwap.__init__ gained `_last_checked_pending_routes` beside this patch's timer, and a neighbouring hunk's context moved. The diff below is regenerated; the change it makes is the same.

